    "title": "Preseason Game Preview #4: New Jersey Devils @ New York Islanders - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matthew Pavlichko ,\n21 hours ago The Matchup: New Jersey Devils (2-0-1) @ New York Islanders (1-2-0) The Broadcast: TV — MSG/Gotham/DAZN, ESPN+, Radio — Devils Hockey Radio. On Thursday night, the Devils faced off against the New York Rangers in the world’s most overrated arena, losing by a score of 4-3 in OT. In the first period, the Devils jumped out to a 1-0 lead, thanks to a power play goal from Stefan Noesen, his first of the preseason, at 8:51. At 12:51 of the second period, Ethan Edwards scored his first goal of the preseason to put the Devils up 2-0, and ultimately send the Devils into the 2nd intermission with a solid lead heading into the third period. Unfortunately for the Devils, the Rangers were not about to give up so easily, and they worked to erase the 2 goal deficit less than 6 minutes into the period. Read full article",
